{"code":"fr","name":"French","native":"Français","phase":1,"medium":"en","file_level":"A2","level":{"title":"Elementary: city, travel, routines, health","goals":["Find your way around a French city","Talk about past trips with passé composé","Describe routines, health, and future plans"],"units":[{"id":"A2-U1","title":"Getting around","lessons":[{"id":"A2-U1-L1","title":"Around the city (going to…)","learn":"Move around: JE VAIS À LA GARE (I go to the station). À melts with LE into AU: AU marché, but À LA banque, À L'hôpital, AUX magasins. Direction words: À GAUCHE (left), À DROITE (right), TOUT DROIT (straight).","vocab":[{"t":"la rue","r":"lah rew","en":"street","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la place","r":"lah plahs","en":"square","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la gare","r":"lah gahr","en":"station","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la banque","r":"lah bah(n)k","en":"bank","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'hôpital","r":"loh-pee-TAHL","en":"hospital","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le magasin","r":"luh mah-gah-ZA(n)","en":"shop","pos":"noun"},{"t":"gauche","r":"gohsh","en":"left","pos":"noun"},{"t":"droite","r":"drwaht","en":"right","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"ALLER + à: au, à la, à l', aux","explain":"JE VAIS = I go, TU VAS = you go, IL VA = he goes. À + LE = AU (au café), À + LA = À LA, À + L' = À L', À + LES = AUX. Four little words, endless journeys!","pattern":"je vais/tu vas/il va + au/à la/à l'/aux + place","examples":[{"t":"Je vais à la gare.","r":"zhuh veh ah lah gahr.","en":"I go to the station."},{"t":"Tu vas au marché?","r":"tew vah oh mahr-SHEH?","en":"Are you going to the market?"},{"t":"Il va à l'hôpital.","r":"eel vah ah loh-pee-TAHL.","en":"He is going to the hospital."}],"mistakes":["Saying À LE café — à + le melts into AU café.","Using VAIS for yourself wrong: JE VAIS, never JE VAS."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Théo","t":"Pardon, où est la gare?","r":"pahr-DOH(n), oo eh lah gahr?","en":"Excuse me, where is the station?"},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Elle est là-bas, à droite.","r":"ell eh lah-BAH, ah drwaht.","en":"It is over there, on the right."},{"sp":"Théo","t":"C'est loin?","r":"seh lwa(n)?","en":"Is it far?"},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Non, c'est près. Cinq minutes.","r":"noh(n), seh preh. sa(n)k mee-NEWT.","en":"No, it is near. Five minutes."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: Where is the station?","answer":"Où est la gare?"},{"type":"fill","q":"Je vais ___ gare. (to the)","answer":"à la"},{"type":"choose","q":"'It is near' is…","options":["C'est loin","C'est près","Il est près","C'est pres"],"answer":"C'est près"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: vais / je / gare / la / à","answer":"je vais à la gare"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Où est la banque?","answer":"Où est la banque?"}],"quiz":[{"q":"JE VAIS À LA GARE means…","options":["I am at the station","I go to the station","my station is big","I like stations"],"answer":1,"why":"Vais + à la = go to."},{"q":"À DROITE is…","options":["left","right","straight","back"],"answer":1,"why":"Droite = right."},{"q":"À + LE becomes…","options":["à le","au","aux","à la"],"answer":1,"why":"À + le melts into AU."},{"q":"OÙ EST LA GARE? means…","options":["Who is at the station?","Where is the station?","How is the station?","What is a station?"],"answer":1,"why":"Où + est = where is."},{"q":"CINQ MINUTES is…","options":["five minutes","ten minutes","five hours","five days"],"answer":0,"why":"Cinq = 5, minutes = minutes."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"City worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to French.","items":["street","station","shop"],"key":["la rue","la gare","le magasin"]},{"instruction":"Complete with au, à la, à l', or aux.","items":["Je vais ___ gare (to the)","Tu vas ___ marché (to the)","Il va ___ magasins (to the)"],"key":["à la","au","aux"]},{"instruction":"Ask for directions.","items":["Where is the bank?","Is it far?"],"key":["Où est la banque?","C'est loin?"]}]}},{"id":"A2-U1-L2","title":"Travel and passé composé","learn":"Talk about finished trips: J'AI VISITÉ (I visited). Passé composé = AVOIR (j'ai, tu as, il a) + past verb (visitÉ, mangÉ, vu). -ER verbs just add É: PARLER → PARLÉ!","vocab":[{"t":"le voyage","r":"luh vwah-YAHZH","en":"trip","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'avion","r":"lah-VYOH(n)","en":"plane","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'hôtel","r":"loh-TELL","en":"hotel","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la valise","r":"lah vah-LEEZ","en":"suitcase","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le billet","r":"luh bee-YEH","en":"ticket","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la plage","r":"lah plahzh","en":"beach","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la montagne","r":"lah moh(n)-TAHN-yuh","en":"mountain","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la photo","r":"lah foh-TOH","en":"photo","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Passé composé: j'ai visité","explain":"J'AI + visitÉ = I visited. TU AS + mangÉ = you ate. IL A + VU = he saw. Most past verbs end in É (from -ER), I (FINI), or U (VENDU, VU, BU).","pattern":"j'ai/tu as/il a + past verb (é/i/u)","examples":[{"t":"J'ai voyagé en Espagne.","r":"zheh vwah-yah-ZHEH ah(n) es-PAHN-yuh.","en":"I travelled in Spain."},{"t":"Tu as acheté des billets?","r":"tew ah ahsh-TEH deh bee-YEH?","en":"Did you buy tickets?"},{"t":"Elle est arrivée hier.","r":"ell eh ah-ree-VEH yehr.","en":"She arrived yesterday. (être verb!)"}],"mistakes":["Saying J'AI VOYAGER — past needs VOYAGÉ, not the infinitive.","Forgetting some verbs use ÊTRE: ELLE EST ARRIVÉE (she arrived)."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Léa","t":"Tu as voyagé cet été?","r":"tew ah vwah-yah-ZHEH set eh-TEH?","en":"Did you travel this summer?"},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Oui, j'ai voyagé au Mexique. J'ai visité la plage.","r":"wee, zheh vwah-yah-ZHEH oh mek-SEEK. zheh vee-zee-TEH lah plahzh.","en":"Yes, I travelled to Mexico. I visited the beach."},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Ça t'a plu?","r":"sah tah plew?","en":"Did you like it?"},{"sp":"Théo","t":"J'ai adoré!","r":"zheh ah-doh-REH!","en":"I loved it!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I travelled in Spain","answer":"J'ai voyagé en Espagne"},{"type":"fill","q":"Tu as acheté des ___? (tickets)","answer":"billets"},{"type":"choose","q":"'She arrived yesterday' uses…","options":["arrive","est arrivée","a arrivé","arrivée a"],"answer":"est arrivée"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: visité / j'ai / plage / la","answer":"j'ai visité la plage"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: J'ai voyagé au Mexique.","answer":"J'ai voyagé au Mexique."}],"quiz":[{"q":"J'AI VISITÉ means…","options":["I visit","I visited","you visited","he visits"],"answer":1,"why":"Ai + É = I did (past)."},{"q":"LA VALISE is…","options":["ticket","suitcase","hotel","beach"],"answer":1,"why":"Valise = suitcase."},{"q":"ÇA T'A PLU? means…","options":["Did you like it?","Do you like it?","Will you like it?","You like it!"],"answer":0,"why":"Past: did it please you."},{"q":"Which is 'you bought'?","options":["j'ai acheté","tu as acheté","il a acheté","acheter"],"answer":1,"why":"Tu as + É = you did."},{"q":"HIER means…","options":["tomorrow","today","yesterday","now"],"answer":2,"why":"Hier = yesterday."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Travel worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to French.","items":["trip","ticket","beach"],"key":["le voyage","le billet","la plage"]},{"instruction":"Put VOYAGER in passé composé.","items":["I travelled","you travelled","she travelled"],"key":["j'ai voyagé","tu as voyagé","elle a voyagé"]},{"instruction":"Answer about a trip.","items":["Did you travel? (yes)","Where? (to Mexico)"],"key":["Oui, j'ai voyagé","J'ai voyagé au Mexique"]}]}}]},{"id":"A2-U2","title":"Life and plans","lessons":[{"id":"A2-U2-L1","title":"Daily routines (reflexive verbs)","learn":"Routines bounce back to you: JE ME LÈVE = I get (myself) up. ME = myself, TE = yourself, SE = himself/herself. Mornings run on ME/TE/SE: se lever, se doucher, se coucher!","vocab":[{"t":"le matin","r":"luh mah-TA(n)","en":"morning","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'après-midi","r":"lah-preh-mee-DEE","en":"afternoon","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le soir","r":"luh swahr","en":"evening","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le travail","r":"luh trah-VAH-yuh","en":"work / job","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'école","r":"leh-KOHL","en":"school","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la douche","r":"lah doosh","en":"shower","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le petit-déjeuner","r":"luh puh-tee-deh-zhuh-NEH","en":"breakfast","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le dîner","r":"luh dee-NEH","en":"dinner","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Reflexive ME/TE/SE: je me lève","explain":"SE LEVER = to get up. JE ME LÈVE, TU TE LÈVES, IL SE LÈVE. The little word before the verb points back at the person — don't drop it!","pattern":"me/te/se + verb","examples":[{"t":"Je me lève à sept heures.","r":"zhuh muh lehv ah set urr.","en":"I get up at seven."},{"t":"Tu te douches le matin?","r":"tew tuh doosh luh mah-TA(n)?","en":"Do you shower in the morning?"},{"t":"Il se couche tard.","r":"eel suh koosh tahr.","en":"He goes to bed late."}],"mistakes":["Saying JE LÈVE without ME — it means 'I lift', not 'I get up'!","Mixing TE and SE: TE = you, SE = he/she."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Théo","t":"Tu te lèves à quelle heure?","r":"tew tuh lehv ah kell urr?","en":"What time do you get up?"},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Je me lève à sept heures et je me douche.","r":"zhuh muh lehv ah set urr eh zhuh muh doosh.","en":"I get up at seven and shower."},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Et tu prends le petit-déjeuner?","r":"eh tew prah(n) luh puh-tee-deh-zhuh-NEH?","en":"And do you eat breakfast?"},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Oui, avec ma famille.","r":"wee, ah-VEK mah fah-MEE.","en":"Yes, with my family."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I get up at seven","answer":"Je me lève à sept heures"},{"type":"fill","q":"Tu te ___? (shower)","answer":"douches"},{"type":"choose","q":"'He goes to bed late' uses…","options":["me couche","te couches","se couche","nous couchons"],"answer":"se couche"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: lève / me / je / heures / sept / à","answer":"je me lève à sept heures"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Je me lève à sept heures.","answer":"Je me lève à sept heures."}],"quiz":[{"q":"JE ME LÈVE means…","options":["I lift it","I get up","I sit down","I run"],"answer":1,"why":"Lève + ME = I get myself up."},{"q":"LE DÎNER is…","options":["breakfast","lunch","dinner","snack"],"answer":2,"why":"Dîner = dinner."},{"q":"À QUELLE HEURE…? asks about…","options":["price","time","place","reason"],"answer":1,"why":"À quelle heure = at what time."},{"q":"TU TE DOUCHES means…","options":["I shower","you shower","she showers","we shower"],"answer":1,"why":"TE = you."},{"q":"Which is reflexive?","options":["je parle","je m'appelle","je mange","je vis"],"answer":1,"why":"Je m'appelle = I call myself."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Routines worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to French.","items":["morning","school","dinner"],"key":["le matin","l'école","le dîner"]},{"instruction":"Complete with me, te, or se.","items":["Je ___ lève (I)","Tu ___ douches? (you)","Il ___ couche (he)"],"key":["me","te","se"]},{"instruction":"Describe your morning.","items":["I get up at …","I shower"],"key":["Je me lève à … heures","Je me douche"]}]}},{"id":"A2-U2-L2","title":"Health and future plans","learn":"At the doctor: J'AI MAL À LA TÊTE = my head hurts. For plans, use FUTUR PROCHE: JE VAIS + verb. JE VAIS VOYAGER = I am going to travel. Easy future, no new endings!","vocab":[{"t":"la tête","r":"lah tet","en":"head","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la main","r":"lah ma(n)","en":"hand","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'œil","r":"luh-yuh","en":"eye","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le médecin","r":"luh mehd-SA(n)","en":"doctor","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la pharmacie","r":"lah fahr-mah-SEE","en":"pharmacy","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la douleur","r":"lah doo-LURR","en":"pain","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la fièvre","r":"lah fyehvr","en":"fever","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la santé","r":"lah sah(n)-TEH","en":"health","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Near future: je vais + verb","explain":"JE VAIS = I go, TU VAS = you go, IL VA = he goes. JE VAIS + verb = I am going to…: JE VAIS MANGER = I am going to eat. The second verb never changes!","pattern":"je vais/tu vas/il va + verb","examples":[{"t":"Je vais voyager.","r":"zhuh veh vwah-yah-ZHEH.","en":"I am going to travel."},{"t":"Tu vas étudier?","r":"tew vah eh-tew-DYEH?","en":"Are you going to study?"},{"t":"Il va pleuvoir.","r":"eel vah pluh-VWAHR.","en":"It is going to rain."}],"mistakes":["Changing the second verb: JE VAIS VOYAGER, never JE VAIS VOYAGE.","Forgetting VAIS: JE vais manger, with VAIS!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Théo","t":"Docteur, j'ai mal à la tête.","r":"dohk-TURR, zheh mahl ah lah tet.","en":"Doctor, my head hurts."},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Tu as de la fièvre?","r":"tew ah duh lah fyehvr?","en":"Do you have a fever?"},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Non, mais je vais me reposer.","r":"noh(n), meh zhuh veh muh ruh-poh-ZEH.","en":"No, but I am going to rest."},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Bien. Tu vas aller bien.","r":"bya(n). tew vah ah-LEH bya(n).","en":"Good. You are going to be fine."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I am going to travel","answer":"Je vais voyager"},{"type":"fill","q":"J'ai mal à la ___. (head)","answer":"tête"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Are you going to study?' is…","options":["Tu vas étudier?","Je vais étudier?","Il va étudier?","Ils vont étudier?"],"answer":"Tu vas étudier?"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: reposer / vais / me / je","answer":"je vais me reposer"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: J'ai mal à la tête.","answer":"J'ai mal à la tête."}],"quiz":[{"q":"JE VAIS VOYAGER means…","options":["I travel now","I travelled","I am going to travel","I want travel"],"answer":2,"why":"Vais + verb = going to."},{"q":"J'AI MAL À LA TÊTE means…","options":["my head hurts","my hand hurts","my eye hurts","my leg hurts"],"answer":0,"why":"Tête = head."},{"q":"LA PHARMACIE is…","options":["hospital","pharmacy","clinic","shop"],"answer":1,"why":"Pharmacie = pharmacy."},{"q":"TU VAS ALLER BIEN means…","options":["you were fine","you are going to be fine","you feel bad","you look fine"],"answer":1,"why":"Vas + aller bien."},{"q":"Which verb NEVER changes in futur proche?","options":["vais","the first verb","the second verb","both verbs"],"answer":2,"why":"Je vais MANGER — manger stays whole."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Health worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to French.","items":["head","doctor","fever"],"key":["la tête","le médecin","la fièvre"]},{"instruction":"Write the plan.","items":["I am going to rest","You are going to be fine"],"key":["Je vais me reposer","Tu vas aller bien"]},{"instruction":"At the doctor.","items":["My head hurts","I have a fever"],"key":["J'ai mal à la tête","J'ai de la fièvre"]}]}}]},{"id":"A2-U3","title":"Shopping and weather","lessons":[{"id":"A2-U3-L1","title":"Clothes and shopping (demonstratives)","learn":"Shop in French! LA CHEMISE, LES CHAUSSURES. Point with CE (this, masculine), CETTE (this, feminine), CES (these): CETTE CHEMISE (this shirt), CE MAGASIN (this shop).","vocab":[{"t":"la chemise","r":"lah shuh-MEEZ","en":"shirt","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le pantalon","r":"luh pa(n)-tah-LOH(n)","en":"trousers","pos":"noun"},{"t":"les chaussures","r":"leh shoh-SEWR","en":"shoes","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la robe","r":"lah rohb","en":"dress","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le magasin","r":"luh mah-gah-ZA(n)","en":"shop","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le prix","r":"luh pree","en":"price","pos":"noun"},{"t":"bon marché","r":"boh(n) mahr-SHEH","en":"cheap","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"cher","r":"shair","en":"expensive","pos":"adjective"}],"grammar":{"title":"CE / CETTE / CES: this and these","explain":"CE + masculine (ce livre), CETTE + feminine (cette chemise), CES + plural (ces chaussures). Before masculine vowel words: CET ami (this friend).","pattern":"ce/cette + thing · ces + things","examples":[{"t":"Cette chemise est bon marché.","r":"set shuh-MEEZ eh boh(n) mahr-SHEH.","en":"This shirt is cheap."},{"t":"Ce magasin est cher.","r":"suh mah-gah-ZA(n) eh shair.","en":"This shop is expensive."},{"t":"Ces chaussures sont jolies.","r":"seh shoh-SEWR soh(n) zhoh-LEE.","en":"These shoes are pretty."}],"mistakes":["Saying CE chemise — chemise is feminine: CETTE chemise.","Saying CE ami — masculine vowel takes CET ami."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Théo","t":"C'est combien, cette chemise?","r":"seh koh(n)-BYA(n), set shuh-MEEZ?","en":"How much is this shirt?"},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Vingt euros. Elle est bon marché.","r":"va(n) uh-ROH. ell eh boh(n) mahr-SHEH.","en":"Twenty euros. It is cheap."},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Et cette robe?","r":"eh set rohb?","en":"And this dress?"},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Cinquante euros.","r":"sa(n)-kah(n)t uh-ROH.","en":"Fifty euros."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: This shirt is cheap","answer":"Cette chemise est bon marché"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ magasin est cher. (this)","answer":"Ce"},{"type":"choose","q":"'These shoes are pretty' is…","options":["Ce chaussures sont jolies","Ces chaussures sont jolies","Cette chaussures est jolie","Les chaussures sont joli"],"answer":"Ces chaussures sont jolies"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: chemise / marché / bon / est / cette","answer":"cette chemise est bon marché"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: C'est combien, cette chemise?","answer":"C'est combien, cette chemise?"}],"quiz":[{"q":"CETTE CHEMISE means…","options":["that shirt","this shirt","those shirts","my shirt"],"answer":1,"why":"Cette = this (feminine)."},{"q":"LE PANTALON is…","options":["shoes","trousers","shirt","dress"],"answer":1,"why":"Pantalon = trousers."},{"q":"BON MARCHÉ means…","options":["good market","cheap","expensive","new"],"answer":1,"why":"Bon marché = cheap (good deal)."},{"q":"CET is used before…","options":["feminine nouns","masculine vowel words","plurals","verbs"],"answer":1,"why":"Cet ami — masculine + vowel."},{"q":"CHER means…","options":["cheap","expensive","big","new"],"answer":1,"why":"Cher = expensive."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Shopping worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to French.","items":["shirt","shoes","cheap"],"key":["la chemise","les chaussures","bon marché"]},{"instruction":"Choose ce, cette, cet, or ces.","items":["___ chemise (this)","___ magasin (this)","___ chaussures (these)"],"key":["cette","ce","ces"]},{"instruction":"Ask prices.","items":["How much is this shirt?","How much is this dress?"],"key":["C'est combien, cette chemise?","C'est combien, cette robe?"]}]}},{"id":"A2-U3-L2","title":"Weather scenes (first imparfait)","learn":"Weather stories use IMPARFAIT: IL FAISAIT BEAU (it was sunny), IL Y AVAIT DU VENT (there was wind). Just two phrases paint any past sky! IL FAISAIT + weather, IL Y AVAIT + thing.","vocab":[{"t":"le soleil","r":"luh soh-LEH-yuh","en":"sun","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la pluie","r":"lah plwee","en":"rain","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le froid","r":"luh frwah","en":"cold","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la chaleur","r":"lah shah-LURR","en":"heat","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'été","r":"leh-TEH","en":"summer","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'hiver","r":"lee-VAIR","en":"winter","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le nuage","r":"luh new-AHZH","en":"cloud","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le vent","r":"luh vah(n)","en":"wind","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"First imparfait: il faisait, il y avait","explain":"IL FAISAIT BEAU/FROID/CHAUD = it was nice/cold/hot. IL Y AVAIT + noun = there was…: IL Y AVAIT DU SOLEIL (there was sun). Weather past = imparfait, always!","pattern":"il faisait + weather · il y avait + thing","examples":[{"t":"Il faisait beau.","r":"eel fuh-ZEH boh.","en":"It was sunny."},{"t":"Il y avait du vent.","r":"eel ee ah-VEH dew vah(n).","en":"There was wind."},{"t":"Il faisait froid hier.","r":"eel fuh-ZEH frwah yehr.","en":"It was cold yesterday."}],"mistakes":["Saying IL A FAIT BEAU for scenes — weather stories use FAISAIT.","Saying IL Y A for past — past needs IL Y AVAIT."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Léa","t":"Quel temps faisait-il hier?","r":"kel tah(n) fuh-ZEH-teel yehr?","en":"What was the weather like yesterday?"},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Il faisait beau. Il y avait du soleil.","r":"eel fuh-ZEH boh. eel ee ah-VEH dew soh-LEH-yuh.","en":"It was sunny. There was sun."},{"sp":"Léa","t":"Et aujourd'hui?","r":"eh oh-zhoor-DWEE?","en":"And today?"},{"sp":"Théo","t":"Il pleut!","r":"eel pluh!","en":"It rains!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: It was sunny","answer":"Il faisait beau"},{"type":"fill","q":"Il y avait du ___ (wind)","answer":"vent"},{"type":"choose","q":"'There was sun' is…","options":["Il y a du soleil","Il y avait du soleil","Il faisait soleil","Il est soleil"],"answer":"Il y avait du soleil"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: beau / faisait / il","answer":"il faisait beau"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Il faisait beau.","answer":"Il faisait beau."}],"quiz":[{"q":"IL FAISAIT BEAU means…","options":["it is sunny","it was sunny","it will rain","it snowed"],"answer":1,"why":"Faisait = was (imparfait)."},{"q":"LA PLUIE is…","options":["sun","rain","wind","cloud"],"answer":1,"why":"Pluie = rain."},{"q":"IL Y AVAIT DU VENT means…","options":["it is windy","there was wind","wind comes","no wind"],"answer":1,"why":"Y avait = there was."},{"q":"Weather in the past uses…","options":["passé composé","imparfait","future","present"],"answer":1,"why":"Scenes = imparfait."},{"q":"QUEL TEMPS FAISAIT-IL? asks…","options":["what time was it?","what was the weather?","where was he?","who came?"],"answer":1,"why":"Quel temps = what weather."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Weather worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to French.","items":["sun","rain","winter"],"key":["le soleil","la pluie","l'hiver"]},{"instruction":"Paint past skies.","items":["It was sunny","There was wind","It was cold yesterday"],"key":["Il faisait beau","Il y avait du vent","Il faisait froid hier"]},{"instruction":"Talk weather.","items":["What was the weather like yesterday?","And today?"],"key":["Quel temps faisait-il hier?","Et aujourd'hui?"]}]}}]}],"test":{"title":"A2 final test","items":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: Where is the station?","answer":"Où est la gare?"},{"type":"fill","q":"J'ai voyagé ___ Mexique (to the)","answer":"au"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I get up at seven'","options":["Je lève à sept heures","Je me lève à sept heures","Je se lève à sept heures","Me lève à sept heures"],"answer":"Je me lève à sept heures"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I am going to study","answer":"Je vais étudier"},{"type":"translate_t","q":"J'ai mal à la tête.","answer":"My head hurts."},{"type":"fill","q":"C'est ___ (near)","answer":"près"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: plu / t'a / ça / ?","answer":"ça t'a plu?"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Où est la banque?","answer":"Où est la banque?"},{"type":"fill","q":"Il ___ beau. (was sunny)","answer":"faisait"},{"type":"choose","q":"'This shirt is cheap'","options":["Ce chemise est bon marché","Cette chemise est bon marché","Ces chemise sont bon marché","Cette chemise bon marché est"],"answer":"Cette chemise est bon marché"}]}}}